      "title": "Is Trading Margin for Volume the Right Housing Bet for Lennar in 2026?",
      "summary": "Lennar Corporation is pursuing a volume-first strategy to navigate persistent housing affordability challenges, with home-sale revenues declining 7% and ASP dropping 5% through August 2026. Despite margin compression, the company achieved meaningful operational gains including 6% construction cost reductions and record 116-day cycle times. With mortgage rates at 7.28%, Lennar expects Q4 deliveries of 22,000-23,000 homes and gross margins of 15.5-16%, betting that cost efficiency and faster production will pay off if affordability improves.",
